---
/**
 * K Culture Wire — **파도의 반감기.** (`/half-life`)
 *
 * ── 왜 ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 *   92편이 「파도가 지나간 뒤 바닥이 높은가」를 묻다가 막혔다 — **신작에는 「전」이 없다.**
 *   문서가 작품과 함께 생기기 때문이다. 서른다섯 편 중 스물아홉이 빠졌다.
 *   ⭐ 그래서 **「전」이 필요 없는 물음**으로 바꿨다 — 봉우리 **뒤**만 본다.
 *
 * ── ⛔ 이 지면이 지키는 것 ────────────────────────────────────
 * ⛔ **「아직 안 떨어졌다」를 「오래 간다」로 안 읽는다.** 봉우리가 지난달이면 모르는 것이다.
 * ⛔ **반감기를 「끝」으로 안 읽는다.** 열여섯 중 열둘이 뒤에 다시 올랐다. 그 표를 같이 싣는다.
 * ⛔ **평균을 앞세우지 않는다.** 중앙값 2달, 평균 2.9달 — 긴 것 몇이 평균을 끈다.
 * ⛔ **얇은 봉우리를 안 쓴다.** 백만분율 한 자리에서 반토막은 잡음이다.
 * ⛔ 광고 자리를 만들지 않는다. Riot Production(App 866800) 승인 전이다.
 *
 * 🔴 Astro 앞말(`---` 사이)은 **TypeScript 다.** JSX 를 넣으면 빌드가 죽는다.
 * 🔴 앞말에서 `export function` 을 쓰지 않는다 — Astro 가 딴 스코프로 옮긴다.
 * 🔴 JSX 는 끝 공백을 버린다. 붙여 써야 할 곳은 `{' '}` 를 넣는다.
 */
import WikiTip from '../../layouts/WikiTip.astro';
import KcwRelatedArticles from '../../components/KcwRelatedArticles.astro';
import KcwCardnews from '../../components/KcwCardnews.astro';
import KcwShorts from '../../components/KcwShorts.astro';
import d from '../../data/wikitip-half-life.json';

const 답 = d.answer;
const 되풀이한것 = d.titles.filter((t) => t.roseAboveHalfAgain);

/* 못 잰 까닭을 묶는다 — 열아홉 줄을 늘어놓으면 안 읽힌다 */
const 까닭별 = [...new Set(d.notMeasured.map((t) => t.why.replace(/only \d+ per million/, 'only N per million')
  .replace(/only \d+ months/, 'only N months')))]
  .map((꼴) => ({
    꼴,
    titles: d.notMeasured.filter((t) => t.why.replace(/only \d+ per million/, 'only N per million')
      .replace(/only \d+ months/, 'only N months') === 꼴),
  }))
  .sort((a, b) => b.titles.length - a.titles.length);

const TITLE = 'A Korean title loses half its readers in two months. Most of them come back at least once';
const DESC =
  `Across four Southeast Asian Wikipedias, ${답.measured} Korean titles could be timed from their `
  + `peak: the median fell below half in ${답.halfLifeMedianMonths} months. `
  + `${답.roseAboveHalfAgain} of them later rose above half again.`;

const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Dataset',
  name: TITLE,
  description: DESC,
  temporalCoverage: d.window,
  creator: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'K Culture Wire' },
  isBasedOn: ['https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/'],
};
---

<WikiTip title={TITLE} description={DESC} jsonLd={jsonLd}
  canonical="https://www.kculturewire.com/half-life">
  <h1>{TITLE}</h1>
  <p class="lead">{d.question}</p>
  <p class="q">
    Of the {답.outOf} titles we hold, {답.measured} have a peak thick enough to time and enough
    months after it to watch. Their median half-life is {답.halfLifeMedianMonths} months.
    {' '}{답.halvedWithinOneMonth} of them lost half their readers in a single month. Not one held
    above half for the whole window.
  </p>

  <section>
    <h2>How long half of it lasts</h2>
    <p class="note">
      Reads are per million reads of that Wikipedia, summed across
      {' '}{d.editions.map((e) => d.editionNames[e]).join(', ')}. We find each title's highest
      month and count forward to the first month below half that value. Window — {d.window}.
    </p>
    <div class="scroll-x">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Title</th><th>Peak</th><th>Peak reads</th><th>Half-life</th>
            <th>Rose above half again</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {d.titles.map((t) => (
            <tr>
              <td class="nm">{t.title}</td>
              <td class="fine">{t.peakMonth}</td>
              <td>{t.peak}</td>
              <td>{t.halfLifeMonths} {t.halfLifeMonths === 1 ? 'month' : 'months'}</td>
              <td class="fine">
                {t.roseAboveHalfAgain
                  ? `${t.returnWaves}× — first after ${t.firstReturnAfterMonths} months`
                  : 'no'}
              </td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p>
      We report the median rather than the mean because the slow tail pulls the mean up — it reads
      {' '}{답.halfLifeMeanMonths} months, which is longer than {d.titles.filter((t) => t.halfLifeMonths < Math.ceil(답.halfLifeMeanMonths)).length}
      {' '}of the {답.measured} titles actually lasted.
    </p>
    {답.stability && 답.stability.verdict.steady && (
      <p class="note">
        ⭐ This median holds. Remove any single title from the {답.measured} above and it stays at
        {' '}{답.stability.median} months — a swing of {답.stability.swingOverMedian}. We check
        every median we publish this way now, after one of ours moved by most of its own size and
        had to be corrected twice in a day; the <a href="/one-out">method is here</a>.
      </p>
    )}
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>The distribution is short and it is not close</h2>
    <div class="scroll-x">
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Half-life</th><th>Titles</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {Object.entries(답.byMonth).sort((a, b) => Number(a[0]) - Number(b[0])).map(([m, n]) => (
            <tr>
              <td class="nm">{m} {m === '1' ? 'month' : 'months'}</td>
              <td>{n}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p>
      Monthly data puts a floor under this. A title that lost half its readers in ten days and one
      that took thirty both read as one month here, so the short end of this table is shorter than
      it looks, not longer.
    </p>
  </section>

  {되풀이한것.length > 0 && (
    <section>
      <h2>A half-life is not an ending</h2>
      <p>
        {되풀이한것.length} of the {답.measured} titles later rose back above half their peak — a
        median of {답.returnWavesMedian} separate times each, the first arriving a median
        {' '}{답.firstReturnMedianMonths} months after the peak. Some of those are new seasons.
        Some are older films finding an audience again years later.
      </p>
      <div class="scroll-x">
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr><th>Title</th><th>Half-life</th><th>Returns</th><th>First return</th>
              <th>Months it came back</th></tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            {되풀이한것.map((t) => (
              <tr>
                <td class="nm">{t.title}</td>
                <td>{t.halfLifeMonths}</td>
                <td>{t.returnWaves}</td>
                <td class="fine">{t.firstReturnAfterMonths} months after peak</td>
                <td class="fine">{t.returnWaveMonths.map((c) => c[0] + (c.length > 1 ? `–${c[c.length - 1]}` : '')).join(', ')}</td>
              </tr>
            ))}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p>
        The half-life counts the first fall, not the last. Read alongside the table above, the
        shape is not a wave that recedes but a wave that recurs — briefly, and more than once.
      </p>
    </section>
  )}

  <section>
    <h2>The {d.notMeasured.length} we could not time</h2>
    <div class="scroll-x">
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Why not</th><th>Titles</th><th>How many</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {까닭별.map((g) => (
            <tr>
              <td class="nm">{g.꼴}</td>
              <td class="fine">{g.titles.map((t) => t.title).join(', ')}</td>
              <td>{g.titles.length}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="note">
      ⚠ The second row is the one to read carefully. A title whose peak was last month has not
      failed to fall — we simply have not watched it long enough. That is unknown, not slow, and
      putting it in the table above would drag the median upward for no reason.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>What this page cannot tell you</h2>
    {d.cannotSay.map((s) => <p class="note">{s}</p>)}
    <p class="note">Reads — Wikimedia Pageviews API, human traffic only, monthly.</p>
  </section>

  <KcwCardnews set="halflife" count={5} />

  <KcwShorts set="halflife"
    says={`A man and a woman read out the median half-life and how many of the titles came back `
      + `above half at least once.`} />

  <KcwRelatedArticles page="/half-life" />
</WikiTip>
